# Entity-First Module Naming

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L1 core naming rule.

## Use This When

- Keep this rule active when creating or renaming feature files.

## Stop Here If

- Stop here once the naming shape is clear; this is a leaf rule.

## Descend To

- No sibling descent required. Apply the naming pattern directly.

Use entity-first modular filenames for feature artifacts to keep related files grouped and discoverable.

## Required naming pattern

- Prefer `<entity>.<artifact>.<ext>` instead of `<artifact>-<entity>.<ext>`.
- Keep all files for one feature near its route/module folder.

## Standard artifacts

- Form UI: `<entity>.form.tsx`
- Server actions: `<entity>.actions.ts`
- Validation schema: `<entity>.schema.ts` or `<entity>.schema.tsx` (match project/file usage)
- View-only component: `<entity>.view.tsx`
- **Client-only module** (Next.js `'use client'` boundary, client mount gates, etc.): `<entity>.client.tsx` (or `<entity>.client.ts` when there is no JSX). Prefer this over ad-hoc names such as `<entity>.shell.tsx`.
- Helpers/utils: `<entity>.utils.ts`
- Constants: `<entity>.constants.ts`
- Types: `<entity>.types.ts`

## Examples

- `profile.form.tsx`
- `profile.actions.ts`
- `profile.schema.tsx`

## Refactoring rule

- For touched modules, prefer renaming old patterns (for example `profile-form.tsx`, `actions.ts`, `schema.ts`) to entity-first names.
- When renaming client-only boundaries, prefer `<entity>.client.tsx` over `*.shell.tsx` (or other vague suffixes).
- After rename, always update imports in the same change.
